# .env.example
#
# Purpose
#   Catalog of every environment variable the app reads. Copy to .env for local
#   development. The real .env is gitignored - never commit secrets.
#   app/config.py is the single Python-side consumer.
#
# When you want a file like this
#   Any service with more than a couple of env vars. It doubles as documentation
#   of the service's configuration surface.
#
# Why it matters
#   - Contributors can copy and fill in instead of guessing variable names.
#   - Empty placeholders for secrets keep the example committable; real values
#     stay out of git via .gitignore.
#   - Sane dev defaults mean copy → fill keys → it runs.
#
# What goes in it
#   - One variable per line in KEY=value form.
#   - A short comment above each group explaining what it controls.
#   - Empty strings for secrets, safe dev defaults for URLs and toggles.
#
# Example (commented; uncomment + edit)
#
# # LLM
# LLM_PROVIDER=echo                       # echo (offline) | anthropic | openai
# LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
#
# # Stores (empty -> in-memory backends for dev/tests)
# REDIS_URL=
# DATABASE_URL=
# VECTOR_BACKEND=memory
#
# # Runtime defense harness (security/)
# HARNESS_ENABLED=true
# CONTROL_MODE=audit                      # audit | human_in_the_loop | block
# CONTRACT_PATH=security/contract.yaml
# HARNESS_API_KEY=
#
# # Observability / alerts
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=
# DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=
#
# # Agent loop guard
# MAX_AGENT_STEPS=4
#
# # MCP - referenced by .mcp.json
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
# SLACK_TEAM_ID=
# PROJECT_ROOT=.
